From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jayden Milne <linux@jayd.ml>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 02:55:38 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/mdp5: Assign pipes again to a plane state restored on
 resume

drm_atomic_helper_suspend() saves the plane states and disables the planes,
which gives their pipes back in the MDP5 global state. The global state is
not saved. drm_atomic_helper_resume() then commits plane states that still
name those pipes, and atomic check keeps them, so the planes run on pipes the
global state calls free.

The next disable finds no owner, and system suspend fails at prepare:

  WARNING: drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/mdp5/mdp5_pipe.c:138 at mdp5_pipe_release+0xd8/0xe8 [msm]
  PM: Some devices failed to suspend, or early wake event detected

A new plane state is a copy of the current one, so it can only name pipes
the current one lacks if it was restored. Drop them in that case, and let
atomic check assign pipes as for any newly enabled plane.

Signed-off-by: Jayden Milne <linux@jayd.ml>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/mdp5/mdp5_plane.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/mdp5/mdp5_plane.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/mdp5/mdp5_plane.c
index adb4d1d50807..45e29409da9b 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/mdp5/mdp5_plane.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/mdp5/mdp5_plane.c
@@ -240,6 +240,14 @@ static int mdp5_plane_atomic_check_with_state(struct drm_crtc_state *crtc_state,
 		if (plane->type == DRM_PLANE_TYPE_CURSOR)
 			caps |= MDP_PIPE_CAP_CURSOR;
 
+		/*
+		 * A state restored on resume names the pipes the plane had before
+		 * suspend, but disabling the plane gave them back in the global
+		 * state. Assign them again.
+		 */
+		if (!to_mdp5_plane_state(old_state)->hwpipe)
+			mdp5_state->hwpipe = mdp5_state->r_hwpipe = NULL;
+
 		/* (re)allocate hw pipe if we don't have one or caps-mismatch: */
 		if (!mdp5_state->hwpipe || (caps & ~mdp5_state->hwpipe->caps))
 			new_hwpipe = true;
